</mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>\u2208</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>\u2212</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are positive in this region.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The only slope field that satisfies the above conditions is the following.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-ffddec792ce1fe9c6e2f5afb23e54d28\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/ffddec792ce1fe9c6e2f5afb23e54d28\"></div> \n</div></div>",
